    "## 9. Applying functions (slides 34–35)\n",
    "- `Series.apply(f)` calls `f` on each value.\n",
    "- `DataFrame.apply(f)` calls `f` on each **column** (a Series) by default; `axis=1` does each row.\n",
    "- `DataFrame.map(f)` calls `f` on every single value. *(The slide's older name, `applymap`, was removed in pandas 3.)*\n",
    "\n",
    "**Predict:** what is the shape of `df`, and what does `df.apply(from_celsius)` give?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "53b903dc",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def from_celsius(temp):\n",
    "    return temp * 9 / 5 + 32\n",
    "\n",
    "df = pd.DataFrame([list(range(0, 100, 10)), list(range(5, 105, 10))])\n",
    "print(df.shape)\n",
    "df.apply(from_celsius)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "31d26261",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# same result, one value at a time (this used to be called applymap)\n",
    "df.map(from_celsius)"
   ]
  },
