    "## 12. Tidy data and pivoting (slides 45–51, textbook \"Pivoting\")\n",
    "**Tidy data:** each variable is a column, each observation is a row. *Long* tables are easy to analyze; *wide* tables are easy to read. `pivot` turns long into wide: you name a column for the **index**, a column for the new **columns**, and a column for the **values**.\n",
    "\n",
    "Start from the percentage of trees with each status in each borough (a Series with a two-level index):"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "10aa7a95",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "pct_per_boro = (trees.groupby([\"borough\", \"status\"]).size()\n",
    "                / trees.groupby(\"borough\").size() * 100)\n",
    "pct_per_boro.head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "11cbb176",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "raises-exception"
    ]
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Predict: will this work? (Quiz question 6!)\n",
    "pct_per_boro.pivot(index=\"borough\", columns=\"status\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "67523c50",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "It raises an error: `pct_per_boro` is a **Series**, and borough and status are in its **index**, not in columns, so there is nothing for `pivot` to use. `reset_index` moves the index into ordinary columns:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "67689928",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "long = pct_per_boro.to_frame().reset_index()\n",
    "long = long.rename(columns={0: \"percentage\"})\n",
    "long.head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "6ca34942",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "wide = long.pivot(index=\"borough\", columns=\"status\", values=\"percentage\")\n",
    "wide.round(1)"
   ]
  },
